  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Use $L=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right)$, where $L$ is the sound level in decibels, $I$ is the sound intensity and $I_0=10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Consider two sound sources. One has 100 times the intensity of the other. What is the difference in their sound levels in decibels?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20\\,\\mathrm{dB}$.",
          "worked": "Let the two intensities be $100I$ and $I$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{100I}{I_0}\\right)-10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right)\\\\\\Delta L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{100I/I_0}{I/I_0}\\right)\\\\\\Delta L&=10\\log_{10}(100)\\\\\\Delta L&=20\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "A car horn has a sound level of about $110\\,\\mathrm{dB}$, while a space shuttle taking off nearby has a sound level of about $150\\,\\mathrm{dB}$. How many times as intense is the sound of the shuttle as the sound of the car horn?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "About $10\\,000$ times as intense.",
          "worked": "Let $I_{\\mathrm{s}}$ be the shuttle sound intensity and $I_{\\mathrm{h}}$ the horn sound intensity. Subtract the sound levels and apply the quotient law.\n$$\\begin{align*}L_{\\mathrm{s}}-L_{\\mathrm{h}}&=150-110\\\\L_{\\mathrm{s}}-L_{\\mathrm{h}}&=40\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}40&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I_{\\mathrm{s}}}{I_{\\mathrm{h}}}\\right)\\\\\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I_{\\mathrm{s}}}{I_{\\mathrm{h}}}\\right)&=4\\\\\\frac{I_{\\mathrm{s}}}{I_{\\mathrm{h}}}&=10^4\\\\\\frac{I_{\\mathrm{s}}}{I_{\\mathrm{h}}}&=10\\,000.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
