        "answer": {
          "short": "All three exceed $90\\,\\mathrm{dB}$. The jet aircraft is at $140\\,\\mathrm{dB}$, the rock concert at $120\\,\\mathrm{dB}$ and the ambulance siren at $100\\,\\mathrm{dB}$.",
          "worked": "For the jet aircraft,\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{100}{10^{-12}}\\right)\\\\L&=10\\log_{10}(10^{14})\\\\L&=140\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the rock concert,\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{10^{-12}}\\right)\\\\L&=10\\log_{10}(10^{12})\\\\L&=120\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the ambulance siren,\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{0.01}{10^{-12}}\\right)\\\\L&=10\\log_{10}(10^{10})\\\\L&=100\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$\nEach level exceeds $90\\,\\mathrm{dB}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
